
Problem Statement
-----------------

Develop a system to detect and recognize handwritten characters on vehicle number plates from images. The goal is to:

- Localize the number plate region in input images (detection).
- Segment individual characters from the localized plate (segmentation).
- Recognize each segmented character using a machine learning model (recognition).

Project Requirements
--------------------

- Input vehicle images in JPG, PNG, or BMP format.
- Detect handwritten number plates under varying lighting, angles, blur, and noise.
- Crop the plate region before character segmentation.
- Segment individual handwritten characters from the cropped plate.
- Recognize each character and output the full plate string.
- Provide confidence scores for each predicted character.
- Include preprocessing, training, inference, and evaluation scripts.
- Report full-plate accuracy, character-level accuracy, confusion matrix, and inference time.

Requirements
------------

- Support images with varying lighting, angles, and noise.
- Handle different handwriting styles and character spacings.
- Provide the final plate string as output and confidence scores per character.

Deliverables
------------

- Code for data preprocessing, plate localization, character segmentation, and recognition.
- Trained model weights and instructions to reproduce training.
- Sample dataset and evaluation script that reports accuracy and per-character metrics.

Evaluation
----------

Evaluate on a held-out test set and report:

- Plate recognition accuracy (full-string match).
- Character-level accuracy and confusion matrix.
- Inference time per image.

Notes
-----

